    </profile>
    <profile name="Living Bomb" typeId="c970-b832-a956-1ac8" typeName="Habilidad" hidden="false" id="d421-bc38-3f2d-7fee">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Descripción" typeId="917b-713d-7c3d-7a9e">Each Spore Mine model is treated as an individual unit. Spore Mines are always ignored for the purposes of any and all mission objectives. Spore Mines are not subject to Instinctive Behaviour, never go to ground (voluntarily or otherwise), run or fall back. At the beginning of the Tyranid Movement phase, each Spore Mine moves D6&quot; in a direction determined by rolling the scatter dice (Tyranid player chooses the direction if a hit is rolled).

If a Spore Mine suffers a wound, touches an enemy model, impassable terrain, or it ends any Movement phase within 2&quot; of an enemy unit, it immediately explodes. Place the central hole of the Área grande marker over the Spore Mine and resolve any hits at Strength 4 and AP 4. Spore Mines that drift off the table or into a friendly unit are immediately removed from play.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Living Battering Ram" typeId="c970-b832-a956-1ac8" typeName="Habilidad" hidden="false" id="1cf6-a779-a032-78d5">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Descripción" typeId="917b-713d-7c3d-7a9e">A Carnifex gains +2 Initiative during a turn in which it launched an Asalto.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
